Z||000000||PocketRocket||09-26-2000||06:06 PM||||I have a 1985 SE V6 wiht a 4 speed manual tranny.  I was driving the other day and went to take off and I had nothing but blue smoke and a bad smell come from the rearend.  The car would not move in any gear at all.  When I try and take off the car just revs up and doesn't move.  Is it the Clutch or did the Tranny go out? Thanks for the help.<P>-----------------<BR>-Larry B<BR>'85 SE 2.8L<p>[This message has been edited by PocketRocket (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||HugGRRRFiero||09-26-2000||08:06 PM||||Been there...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I've got a 2.5L 4 speed manual.  Last summer about a month after I got mine my clutch took a dump.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Coming to an intersection I pushed in and held the clutch, put the tranny into 1st just as I was rolling probably going less than 5 mph.  The car jerked as if I had let out of the clutch.  As I let out on the clutch to get the car going again from a stop, weird noises were coming from behind my seat and a real funky smell was telling me ut oh.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  I had the same thing, I could put the car in all the gears but no go, just vroom vroom.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Well, sorry for the story of one of my DNF's, I'd say you will need a new clutch, throwout bearing, etc.<P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">         <BR>         <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by HugGRRRFiero (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||3
